pat dry
 - 2.5 lbs pork chops (approx. 4 1 inch thick bone-in)

season with
 
 - 1 tsp garlic powder
 - 1/2 tsp smoked paprika
 - 1/2 tsp black pepper

set to skillet on medium-high heat
add
 - oil 
add meat
sear for 2–3 minutes per side until golden brown transfer to the slow cooker
combine in hot pan
 - 10.5 oz condensed cream of mushroom
 - 1/2 cup chicken broth 
 - 1 tbsp Worcestershire
top pork chops with
 - 8 oz sliced white mushrooms
 - 1 chopped onion
top with sauce
cook 4-6 hours on low until tender
set meat aside
purée sauce if desired
combine with water
 - 1 tbsp corn startch
stir into sauce
return meat
cook on high 15 minutes 
stir every 5 minutes
serve with rice or egg noodles 

serves 4

